    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Information-Officer_JR27303": {
      "title": "Information Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The primary function of the Information Officer position is to guarantee an effective public relations environment for the Office of Undergraduate Admissions. The Admissions Office receives nearly 60,000 visitors, countless phone calls and emails annually.   The Information Officer is a high impact position due to the number of contacts that the incumbent has with various University constituents including current students, faculty, staff, prospective and admitted students, parents, college counselors, alumni and friends of Georgetown.  The person in the position must be aware of the current happenings on campus and must also be able to handle callers, visitors and emails with a variety of issues.  Oftentimes the incumbent will be called upon to help with difficult calls or situations which need to be managed with sensitivity.  The incumbent should be able to answer all but the most complex admissions questions, accurately articulate admissions office policy, know important deadlines and think critically to solve problems including public relations issues.  Work Interactions The person in the position must be able to manage the nearly 60,000 visitors that come to campus to attend an information session and campus tour.  The incumbent must also coordinate with the admissions officers to help with campus visitors.  Maintaining and monitoring the flow of visitors is essential especially during our high-volume times of year.  In addition, the incumbent assists all visitors and callers to the office in a courteous manner, answers all email inquiries, accurately codes information from phone calls and campus visits and assists with special projects as needed.  The position requires occasional weekend work. This position reports to the Director of Campus Programs but must work with all other areas of the office including Operations, Alumni Admissions and Admissions Officers. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required College admissions experience or special training in a college/educational environment is highly desired. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On Campus . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $20.16 - $31.30 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Community-Director--Village-A_JR27280-1": {
      "title": "Community Director, Village A",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Community Director in Residential Education at Georgetown University administers the residential program for a campus community housing between 225-600 students. The Community Director’s primary role is to foster the holistic development of students through active engagement and mentoring of students in the residential education experience. Duties include supervision and development of the Resident Assistant or Resident Fellow staff and the design of cultural, educational, and social programming supporting the formation of students in the Jesuit tradition. The Community Director, in partnership with the Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow staff, educates students through the development of Educational Plans, promotion of leadership development, partnerships with Faculty and Resident Ministers, emergency response, and through community investment in an established code that emphasizes respect for self and others.  The Community Director manages the occupancy, safety, and security of the residential area they oversee. The Community Director is a critical member of Georgetown’s Safety Net and works closely with the Georgetown University Police Department and other Student Affairs offices to respond to student emergencies, including mental health crises, facility emergencies, injury, and other concerns. The Community Director serves on an emergency response duty rotation and responds to significant student issues. During the summer months, Community Directors play a vital role in creating and planning departmental programs and services while supporting the residential conference and intern housing operations. Community Directors are expected to serve as positive ambassadors of the University and Residential Living mission, vision, and values within their teams, communities, and across campus. The Community Director primarily performs desk work in an office or workspace using a university issued computer. Some meetings or events occur in other buildings on the Hilltop or Capitol Campus or occasionally at off campus locations. This position is required to live on campus and participate in an on-call/on-site duty rotation 24-hours a day, 365 days a year. The Community Director must be able to respond quickly to emergencies (behavioral, health related, and facility/physical plant) and other needs when they arise. Work Interactions Community Directors supervise the student Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow team and lead all community development and student formation initiatives within their assigned community. The Community Director provides mediation services to students, supervision to Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow staff, developmental guidance to students, and feedback to departmental leadership. On a daily basis the Community Director schedules student meetings and is readily available to student staff and colleagues. The Community Director is expected to communicate in a timely manner with faculty, staff, parents, and others regarding shared concerns about students.  Requirements and Qualifications A completed Master's Degree is required, preferably in the area of Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or Social Work. Thorough understanding of and commitment to the work of Residential Living as well as the education and character development of college students is expected. Demonstrated experience in the areas of leadership, supervision, professional development, administrative skills, social justice and inclusion, community development, educational engagement, and emergency response. Ability to manage stress, conflict, and frustration constructively; demonstrate a positive attitude. Identify, define, and apply creative and original approaches to resolving issues and use sound judgment based on training and departmental policies and protocol. An awareness and understanding of the Jesuit values and the ability to conceptualize them in the application of this role. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Emergency Employee This position has been designated as an emergency position. Because many services provided by the University are required seven days a week on a twenty-four hour basis, the University makes every effort to remain open at all times. This position must always report to work on time regardless of weather conditions, whether the University is closed or not. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $41,926.00 - $65,090.00 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Healy-4th-Floor/Director-for-Finance-and-Operations---Georgetown-University_JR27262": {
      "title": "Director for Finance and Operations - Georgetown University",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview This position is responsible for all aspects of budget and financial operations for one of the two large groups of clusters of Main Campus Administrative Units. The incumbent will hold a key position on the Main Campus Administrative Units Finance Team, reporting directly to the Senior Business Manager (“SBM”).  He/she has a direct oversight of a Sr. Financial Analyst and an indirect oversight of an Associate Director of Finance & Ops.  Director is responsible for all annual budget activities, including top-down and detailed budget development and forecasting, for monitoring the actual performance of the units against the budget, for financial operations, and for the year-end close activities for the assigned units with an annual expense budget exceeding $70M. In addition, responsibilities include review and oversight of HCM transactions as a Finance Partner (in conjunction and under guidance of the Senior Business Manager), planning for and monitoring of the restricted funds and research expenditures as directed by the SMB and the CFO of Main Campus. The Director will work with procurement and or accountants on a regular basis. Work Interactions The Director for Finance & Ops will report directly to the Senior Business Manager (SBM) for the Administrative Units on Main Campus and will work closely with the SBM on operational, planning and strategic matters of the units he/she is responsible for.  The position holder will be in close contact with the Unit Heads that his/her team supports. This position interacts with many university departments, which requires excellent customer service and communication skills and the ability to work with a wide range of constituents, such as Deans, Vice Provosts, Department heads, faculty, the Joint Office of Research Administration, Advancement, and various offices under the OCFO, for example, Accounts Payable, Payroll Services, General Accounting, and other.  The incumbent works closely with the Provost Office Finance Team. The Director will regularly collaborate with other Associate Directors, Directors and SBMs from Schools and be part of the Main Campus Financial Operations Working Group.  The incumbent will interact with the Campus CFO and other leaders of Main Campus.  Requirements and Qualifications A Bachelor’s degree is required.  Master’s degree in economics, finance, business or accounting is strongly preferred.  A Bachelor’s degree plus substantial experience in closely related fields may substitute for a Master’s degree. 10+ years' of progressive work experience in financial analysis and budgeting in a sophisticated office environment. Relevant financial acumen (budgeting, transactional support, revenue-generating activities, chart of accounts, journals, requisitions, purchase orders, procurement, and travel) Ability to build and utilize financial reports Advanced business analytics skills Ability to support the establishment and management of budgets of $70M+ Strong leadership skills coupled with proven team management abilities. Prior experience working with complex teams Excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills Ability to engage regularly with internal and external stakeholders, including unit leads and administrators across the institution Strong organizational and time management skills; proficiency managing and prioritizing multiple tasks Ability to work with a variety of financial systems, with prior experience preferred in Workday, and Adaptive Ability to interpret the strategic goals and plan for assigned units Revenue and expenditure analysis experience Prior experience with complex financial and longitudinal planning and financial forecasting Adaptability and flexibility Attention to detail Ability to triage and solve complex challenges and requests Proficiency in the Microsoft Office suite, with a mastery of excel and experience with managing and analyzing large volumes of data Service oriented, professional demeanor and a team orientation is required; i.e. avoiding “that’s not my job” Ability to work well under pressure, in a high paced environment Ability to think outside the box and to solve problems creatively Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Telework. The work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $80,429.00 - $157,238.93 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Director-of-Financial-Operations--Dean-s-Office---Georgetown-University-College-of-Arts---Sciences_JR27276": {
      "title": "Director of Financial Operations, Dean's Office - Georgetown University College of Arts & Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Director of Financial Operations , in partnership with the Managing Finance Director, is responsible for the financial planning and management, and the business operations and analysis, of The Georgetown College of Arts & Sciences (CAS). The Director of Financial Operations also leads the financial operations team for the CAS and partners with financial services team that provide support to CAS. The Director of Financial Operations works closely with the Managing Finance Director to ensure that the financial planning, management, and administration of the CAS aligns with the school’s mission and objectives. This position is responsible for the creation, submission, implementation, execution and analysis of the CAS’ detailed expense and revenue budgets. The Director of Financial Operations communicates data-supported financial trends, projections, and other KPIs to leadership and various decision-makers within CAS, Main Campus (Provost’s Office), and University level. This position is responsible for collaborating with school and campus leadership, along with other campus partners, to strategize on best practices, system and operational enhancements, and change management. This position participates in analysis and problem resolution involving financial, administrative, and policy matters affecting the CAS. The Director of Financial Operations serves as representative for the CAS on cross-school and campus committees and other forums, providing input for university partners for decision making, as well as advocating for the interests of, and providing perspective from, the CAS. This position also serves as consultant for the CAS’ various stakeholders in interpreting and implementing changes to policy, procedures, or system/business operations. The Director of Financial Operations assists in implementing effective internal controls and overseeing adherence to University business policies and procedures.  The Director of Financial Operations will provide exceptional customer support to departments by accurately anticipating and/or identifying needs, troubleshooting issues, and executing effective resolutions in a timely manner and in compliance with promulgated policies. This position provides, and/or advises on, training to various administrators within the CAS. The Director of Financial Operations will be an expert on, and ensure compliance with, university, campus, and school policies, procedures, and best practices, and will maintain a thorough understanding of the GMS Chart of Accounts fields, values, and how they interrelate. This position will also be expected to be knowledgeable on pertinent regulatory information in regards to sponsored activity, both generally, and with specific sponsors. Work Interactions The Director of Financial Operations reports directly to the Managing Finance Director. The Director of Financial Operations supervises 4+ full-time employees and manages the relationships of the “dotted-line” teams supporting CAS (including Accounting, Procurement.) The position also works closely with the CAS’ department chairs, program directors, and departmental administrators.  This position works with, and/or advises, members of the CAS Finance office on a number of critical tasks relating to the financial operations of the CAS, including, but not limited to: annual budget development and analysis, monthly reconciliations, continuous and in-depth department and faculty support for all matters and inquiries related to finance and budget, maintenance of faculty research accounts (both internal funds and external/sponsored funds), post-award administration for sponsored grants, monthly forecasting of revenue and expense trends, approval of all financial transactions in accordance with developed budget, university policy, and, if applicable, sponsor requirements, and position budget/compensation analysis and review. This position interacts with many University departments, requiring excellent customer service skills and the ability to work with a wide range of constituents. These constituents include: department chairs and administrators in 26 academic departments and 12+ interdisciplinary programs, the Provost’s Office of Finance and Business Services, Join Office of Research Administration, Sponsored Programs Financial Operations, Accounts Payable, Payroll Services, General Accounting, Advancement, Gift Accounting, Billing and Payment Services, and other partners within University Financial Affairs. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree strongly preferred (MBA or similar). 7+ years' progressive work experience in financial analysis and budgeting in a complex environment; preferably in a university or other non-profit setting.  Excellent written and oral communication skills.  Mastery of Excel (vlookups, pivot tables, macros, etc.). Ability to develop innovative approaches and adapt to changes in policies and technologies. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and meet time-sensitive deadlines.   Ability to interpret and apply university policies and procedures within complex and diverse organization. Strong orientation to detail and deadlines.  Strong desire to achieve results. Excellent customer service skills. Ability to work well under pressure and function as a team player. Possess poise, diplomacy and confidence to handle complex situations, especially those of a confidential nature and in interactions with senior University administrators. Proficiency with Georgetown University systems including GMS (Workday) and Adaptive Planning preferred. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Cover letter and resume required for consideration. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $80,429.00 - $157,238.93 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Graduate-Program-Coordinator--Department-of-Government---Georgetown-University-College-of-Arts---Sciences_JR27245": {
      "title": "Graduate Program Coordinator, Department of Government - Georgetown University College of Arts & Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Graduate Program Coordinator (a one-year renewable term position) is responsible for supporting the academic, administrative, operational, enrollment management, and strategic communication functions of assigned graduate programs within the College of Arts and Sciences, primarily but not limited to the M.A. in Conflict Resolution. The Graduate Program Coordinator reports to the Business Manager with a dotted line to the Program Director and collaborates closely with faculty, university offices, students, alumni, and external stakeholders to advance program goals and operations. This position serves as a key operational and strategic partner in managing the day-to-day functions of assigned programs, with responsibilities spanning enrollment management, admissions and merit aid administration, marketing and communications, student and faculty support, event coordination, and program operations. The incumbent designs and implements recruitment and yield strategies to support enrollment goals, manages admissions workflows and communications, and oversees digital outreach efforts including website management, social media, marketing materials, and public relations initiatives to raise program visibility and engagement. The role also requires awareness of financial policies, program expenditures, and the operational implications of budget-related decisions associated with events, financial aid, and other program activities. In collaboration with the department’s Administrative Coordinator, the Graduate Program Coordinator also supports academic and administrative operations by coordinating course scheduling and registration processes, assisting with program assessment and reporting, supporting research and student engagement activities, and ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures. In addition, the position plans and executes special events such as orientations, commencement activities, academic programming, alumni engagement events, and recruitment initiatives while monitoring budgets and operational logistics. The role requires strong collaboration, organizational, communication, analytical, and project management skills, as well as the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic academic environment. Duties may also include broader program support functions related to alumni relations, community development, and other operational needs as assigned by program leadership. Work Interactions This position reports to the Department Business Manager and Program Director and works closely with the department’s staff, faculty, students, and alumni. The incumbent will call, email, and meet with prospective and current students. They will work closely with all functional areas within the College Dean’s Office staff as well as prospective students, current students, alumni, vendors/suppliers, industry connections, and many other audiences. The incumbent will liaise with other Georgetown University offices such as Graduate Admissions, University Registrar, Office of Global Services, Student Financial Services and Financial Affairs and other academic units. The incumbent should demonstrate a proactive and adaptable approach to their work, remaining responsive to the evolving needs of the program and university community. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. 2-3 years of relevant experience, preferably in higher education. Commitment to student success as part of an equitable and diverse community. Working knowledge of enrollment management and admissions best practices. Exceptional communication skills in writing, editing, public speaking, and customer service. Strong analytical, financial, and documentation skills; experience using data to understand historical trends to drive and support decision making, linking strategies to outcomes. A self-starter with a proven ability to collaborate and develop best-in-class business models, systems, and procedures to support an exceptional student experience. Events management experience. An ability to understand the nuanced needs and characteristics of this specialized academic program, and the ability to authentically articulate the unique opportunities and value. Understanding of social media and emerging media tools to utilize in recruitment and branding of the program. Organized, and proactive; highly responsive, flexible, and adaptable.  Technical aptitude and the ability to pick up new technology quickly.     Understanding of appropriate and confidential communication, file management, and storage. Proficiency with Google Apps, WordPress or other web editing tools, and the Adobe Suite (Acrobat, Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, and Premier Pro) Preferred Qualifications Experience in graduate program management. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Cover letter and resume required for consideration. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $47,586.00 - $87,558.13 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Administrative-Assistant--Department-of-Linguistics---Georgetown-University-College-of-Arts---Sciences_JR27251": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Department of Linguistics - Georgetown University College of Arts & Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Administrative Assistant, Department of Linguistics, the College of Arts and Sciences – Georgetown University (a one-year renewable term position) , provides a range of support functions for Distinguished University Professor Deborah Tannen, who is an internationally known author, speaker, and public intellectual in the fields of language, communication, and gender. This includes managing Dr. Tannen’s social media presence and website; answering, mostly by email but also by phone and regular mail, all inquiries, requests, and invitations to give interviews, answer questions, and speak at or attend events; tasks related to Dr. Tannen’s teaching; and other tasks as they arise. Duties include but are not limited to: Aforementioned correspondence and inbox management Assisting in preparation and maintenance of graduate and undergraduate courses Processing requests for permission to reprint Dr. Tannen’s work Arranging speaking engagements and travel Research in relation to Dr. Tannen’s writing Maintaining office files and organization Work Interactions The person in this position represents Deborah Tannen, the Linguistics Department, and Georgetown University to a wide range of individuals within and outside the University. Positive impact includes ensuring that all who approach the office go away with a positive impression, even when their requests cannot be fulfilled. The incumbent makes it possible for Dr. Tannen to be more available to Georgetown students and colleagues, and more productive in research and writing, which brings positive attention to the university. Conversely, errors or poor performance could potentially result in Georgetown and non-Georgetown individuals going away with a negative impression. The position reports directly to Dr. Tannen. Requirements and Qualifications High School Diploma and 2-4 years of experience in a professional environment required (or equivalent combination of education and work experience). The position requires a person who is a consummate professional with exemplary interpersonal skills, writes well, is detail-oriented, can manage multiple tasks with minimal supervision, and is happy to work independently. Must have superior organizational skills and proven experience working independently.  Must have a proven ability to work responsibly with highly confidential materials, as well as ability to balance and prioritize several assignments at one time. Outstanding written/oral communication skills essential. Good working knowledge of PC operation required.  Must have experience in the use of state-of-the-art software applications, including MS Word and Power Point. Must also know or be willing to learn how to use Squarespace and other web-based platforms. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from a four-year institution. Familiarity with academic and publishing environments is helpful. Previous experience working in a university environment a plus. Knowledge of Georgetown systems and locations a plus. Experience in an office setting and interest in higher education highly desired. Knowledge of Canvas highly desired. Baseline knowledge of linguistics and academic research skills highly desired. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Cover letter and resume required for consideration. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $19.20 - $28.70 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/2121-Wisconsin-Avenue/Controller_JR27273": {
      "title": "Controller",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Controller is a vital executive leader within the Office of the Chief Financial Officer (OCFO), serving as a strategic thought partner and advisor to the CFO on university-wide financial policy, operational strategy, and long-term fiscal health. In addition to driving core accounting and financial operations, the Controller plays a pivotal role in shaping and implementing the OCFO Strategic Plan—focusing on exemplary financial stewardship, process optimization, digital transformation, and fostering collaborative partnerships across academic and administrative divisions. Reporting directly to the CFO, the Controller provides executive oversight for a comprehensive financial portfolio, including financial accounting and GAAP reporting, internal controls, external audit management, tax, student accounts and receivables, and post-award sponsored projects administration (including Uniform Guidance compliance). Through active engagement with the Board of Trustees, campus business officers, and executive leadership, the Controller aligns day-to-day operations with the university’s overarching institutional goals. Work Interactions OCFO Leadership: Maintains a close advisory relationship with the CFO and the OCFO management team. Collaborates closely and seamlessly with the Budget & Financial Planning & Analysis division to align operational accounting with long-term fiscal modeling and resource allocation. Works in direct tandem with Investment, Legal, Human Resources, Facilities, Auxiliary Services, and Risk Management. Academic & Unit Leadership: Provides regular financial guidance and consultation to Campus Vice Presidents of Finance, Chief Business Officers (CBOs), Deans, and unit administrators. Governance: Interacts directly with members of the Board of Trustees/Directors (specifically the Audit and Finance & Administration Committees). External Partners: Serves as the primary institutional representative to external audit teams, financial institutions, actuarial consultants, and federal/state regulatory authorities. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Finance, Accounting or related discipline required. Minimum 10 years of progressively responsible financial management experience, including demonstrated leadership in a complex organization (higher education or non-profit sector strongly preferred). CPA certification required. Preferred Knowledge and Skills Strategic Vision: Demonstrated experience serving as a strategic advisor to executive management, with a track record of connecting financial operations to institutional goals. Higher Education Expertise: In-depth knowledge of university accounting principles, fund accounting, Uniform Guidance, F&A rate proposals, and academic budget models. Leadership & Team Building: Proven ability to mentor, supervise, and inspire a diverse team of professionals while fostering a collaborative, customer-service-oriented culture. Technical Acumen: High degree of comfort leveraging financial systems, business intelligence platforms, and modern enterprise resource planning (ERP) technology. Communication & Influence: Exceptional written, verbal, and interpersonal skills; ability to articulate complex financial concepts clearly to non-financial stakeholders, senior executives, and board members. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $167,633 - $400,000 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Car-Barn/Director-of-Graduate-Fellowships-and-Awards_JR27179": {
      "title": "Director of Graduate Fellowships and Awards",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Director of Graduate Fellowships and Awards at Georgetown’s University Office of Graduate Studies is responsible for the overall development, application, expansion and training in relation to external awards, including sponsored government and non-government research awards, fellowships, foundation fellowships, private grants, and other external awards to graduate students across various programs, including Biomedical Sciences at the GUMC and the Law Center. This position plays a crucial role in helping graduate students to secure external financial support to enhance their academic and research endeavors. By increasing the number and monetary value of external awards obtained at Georgetown, the Director contributes to the university's strategic goal of supporting scholarly excellence and fostering national recognition as well as to the University’s financial position. This Director is also tasked with overseeing internal awards at Georgetown, through managing a faculty committee, and facilitating the review process for internal grants and awards. These include research travel grants and the other internal fellowships important to both research and the University’s mission, the Healy awards. The role includes finding and promoting funding opportunities for graduate students through advertising, newsletters, website, social media, workshops, and holding informational sessions in the various schools. The position works closely with all graduate students at Georgetown, to educate them on fellowships, including developing and running a summer, zero credit, optional training course for graduate students on obtaining grant funding.  The Director will serve as the Project Director for federally funded fellowship programs and oversee the management of awards in partnership with JORA. A critical role of the Director is to develop, build and maintain relationships with a wide range of external funding organizations, government sources and program directors, and foundations. Graduate Professionalization Program: Develop, manage, and teach an optional University-wide graduate professionalization course, The Graduate Professionalization Seminar, designed to prepare graduate students for success in academic and professional careers. The seminar will cover topics such as effective university teaching (including instructor preparation, classroom management, grading practices, and student support), research success (including conference presentations, abstract writing, publication strategies, and scholarly networking), research integrity, career planning, and professional skills. The course will be offered through the University Office of Graduate Studies as part of its graduate student enrichment portfolio. In addition, the Office will develop and maintain a customizable Canvas course, accompanying instructional materials, and faculty training resources that can be adopted and adapted by individual schools, departments, and programs across Georgetown to meet their own graduate professionalization needs. Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Develop strategies to expand grant and fellowship opportunities and funding. Collaborate with faculty, staff and students, to enhance funding opportunities and support applications. Cultivate relationships with government and non-government funding agencies and foundations, and donors. Monitor external funding trends and recommend and implement strategies to increase competitiveness. Manage the “Office of Graduate Fellowships & Awards” website, newsletters, and develop and maintain an awards database and website. Create and teach a zero credit funding and grant-writing course. Work Interactions This position reports to the Assistant VP for Grad Student Enrichment. This position also will work closely with Georgetown’s Office of Advancement and Corporate and Foundation Relations, the Graduate Career Center, , the Joint Office for Research Administration, the Office of Regulatory Affairs, Sponsored Accounting, the Office of the Provost, the Biomedical Graduate Education office, Research Development Services office, , Center for Research and Fellowships, the Office of the Registrar, the Military and Veterans’ Services Center, and the Office of the Chief Research Officer,  as well as departmental chairs, Directors of Graduate Studies, administrators, and principal investigators who are directly involved with graduate student fellowship, grant, and other sponsored award funding. This position also works closely with the Graduate Admissions Team to contribute to comprehensive recruitment plans for prospective applicants, including a communications plan for accepted or admitted applicants.  This position will be the point of contact or liaison with varied federal funding agencies and organizations such as the U.S. Department of Education, the U.S. State Department’s Fulbright Scholars Program, the National Institutes of Health, the U.S. Department of Defense Awards Program, and the National Science Foundation amongst others; as well as all other relevant federal and private foundations. This position also provides program management support for the cross-campus Graduate Studies Research Steering Committee (GRSC), composed of faculty members and some academic professionals who are assigned to specific program reviews; in some cases, this position may also be called upon to convene the GSRSC to consider new policies governing competitions or to revise awarding criteria or review processes, to align with industry best practices. In this capacity, this position oversees the committee, including the dissemination of application materials, chairing review panels, and managing award-related communications and all other committee-related matters.  This position is responsible for fostering strong relationships with graduate students across Georgetown, providing guidance and support throughout their academic and professional journeys. The role provides ongoing guidance through helping students navigate funding opportunities, improve their grant-writing skills, and access the resources necessary for their academic and professional success. This position will also serve as the PI or PD on certain institutional submissions, as well as serve as the application manager in Research.gov, G5/6, IRIS.gov, etc. on behalf of student applicants applying to various federal competitions. Occasionally, the individual also may be called upon to serve on ad hoc reviews or to help facilitate reviews or mock reviews for the Center for Research & Fellowships (CFR), serving the undergraduate population. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 7 -10 years of progressive grant and contract experience required. Master’s degree preferred; Extensive experience with grant applications and funding management required; Ph.D. desirable. Strong writing, communication, and editing skills; experience with designing or leading workshops essential Service-oriented attitude, especially with respect to students Ability to manage multiple projects within a given timeframe Excellent attention to details  Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $66,783.00 - $126,720.23 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Medical-Center/Clinical-Trials-Manager_JR27162": {
      "title": "Clinical Trials Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Clinical Trials Manager, Department of Neurology/Memory Disorders – Georgetown University. Participates in clinical trial set up, execution, documentation, education/recruitment, and provides general data management of the most complex clinical studies in the Department of Neurology, Memory Disorders Program. As clinical trials manager, responsibilities include review and mastery of clinical research documents (protocols, case report forms, reports and statistical analysis), monitoring recruitment and retention, adherence to study visit schedule, timely data entry (develops data management plans), compliance with all study procedures including close-out and training of other staff members on protocol measures and GU clinical research policies as needed. Responsible for patient cognitive testing (minimum two-years cognitive testing experience necessary), caregiver communication and interview, chart review and data organization using various web-based databases. The Clinical Trials Manager will also prepare for and facilitate research and monitoring visits as well as administer cognitive testing to subjects. The incumbent will manage multiple local and multi-center clinical trials and will need to be detail-oriented with a solid base of management skills and interpersonal skills. The individual is expected to have working knowledge of compliance policies with respect to the clinical regulatory environment and requires little to no supervision to perform all job functions. Acts as liaison with clinicians, pharmaceutical companies and the federally-funded Alzheimer’s Disease Research Institute (ATRI) to implement studies and to meet all data timelines, in part to ensure timely and accurate study payments to GU. Corresponds directly with study sponsors to facilitate subject participation, submits subject visit information and resolves data queries. The position will provide support to the Principal Investigator (PI), co-investigators and all other study collaborators for neurology clinical trials. The manager is also responsible for maintaining and facilitating regulatory documents, including IRB submissions, together with the Regulatory Manager. The clinical trials manager will also prepare dynamic training guides to promote seamless onboarding for new staff members in the Memory Disorders Program and will work diligently – including troubleshooting for all Memory Disorders staff- within the OnCore system to manage study visit data and study visit payments to participants. The manager will be required to obtain and retain all necessary certifications in order to perform the position effectively. Work Interactions Works as part of a team to establish effective management of clinical trials within the Department of Neurology, Memory Disorders Program. Recruit, conduct, establish and organize, document and maintain approval for these trials. The position will provide support to the Principal Investigator (PI), co-investigators and all other study collaborators for Memory Disorders Program clinical trials. Works with PIs, fellows, subjects and team members to conduct safe, accredited clinical trials in the Department of Neurology. Operates with a strong understanding of current GU policies and SOPs related to research and compliance. Works under the direct supervision of the Research Director Neurology/Memory Disorders. This position also requires interaction with patients, sponsors and CROs. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s or Master’s degree and 3-5 years of experience or equivalent relevant work experience; e.g. each year or work experience may be substituted for each year of education required Excellent organizational and communication skills with ability to work independently and collaboratively with investigators and subjects Attention to detail is critical and must be self-directed with a solid base of management skills. Must be able to manage multiple tasks Must be able to demonstrate successful track records using analytical, organizational and problem-solving skills Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to communicate professionally and clearly. Solids writing skills include grammar, punctuation, composition and spelling. Computer proficiency essential, with demonstrated knowledge of PC software programs including Windows, MS Office, internet and email. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website:https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $44,022.00 - $73,406.80 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Washington-DC/Occupational-Safety-Manager_JR26933": {
      "title": "Occupational Safety Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Occupational Safety Manager is responsible for developing, implementing, and managing comprehensive occupational safety and health programs that support compliance with applicable OSHA regulations, District of Columbia requirements, industry best practices, and Georgetown University policies. Reporting to the Director of Fire Prevention and Occupational Safety, the position serves as the University's subject-matter expert in occupational safety and provides leadership in hazard identification, risk assessment, incident prevention, regulatory compliance, and safety program development. The Occupational Safety Manager oversees occupational safety initiatives for Planning and Facilities Management (PFM), including capital construction projects, small projects, maintenance operations, shops, and other University activities with occupational safety risks. The incumbent conducts inspections, audits, and assessments to identify hazards, evaluate compliance, and recommend corrective actions that reduce risk and promote a safe and healthy work environment for employees, contractors, students, and visitors. The position works collaboratively with University departments, project managers, contractors, consultants, and other stakeholders to ensure the effective implementation of safety requirements across all phases of construction, renovation, maintenance, and operations. Responsibilities include reviewing contractor safety plans, conducting jobsite inspections, monitoring compliance with University safety standards, and recommending corrective actions when deficiencies are identified. The Occupational Safety Manager develops, implements, and maintains occupational safety programs and written procedures, including but not limited to Lockout/Tagout (LOTO), Confined Space Entry, Fall Protection, Walking-Working Surfaces, Personal Protective Equipment (PPE), Hazard Communication, Ladder Safety, Contractor Safety, and other OSHA-required programs. The position is responsible for conducting program evaluations and ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and industry best practices. A significant responsibility of the position is to develop and deliver occupational safety training and awareness programs for University employees, supervisors, and contractors. The incumbent conducts classroom, field, and online training; develops educational materials; maintains training records; and promotes a proactive safety culture through engagement, communication, and continuous improvement initiatives. The Occupational Safety Manager leads and supports investigations into occupational injuries, illnesses, near-misses, property damage incidents, and contractor-related events. Responsibilities include conducting root cause analyses, identifying contributing factors, developing corrective and preventive actions, tracking trends, and providing recommendations to reduce future risk. The position manages the Planning and Facilities Management Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) Program, including hazard assessments, PPE selection, implementation, employee training, compliance monitoring, and program evaluation. The incumbent also develops safety performance metrics, analyzes injury and incident trends, prepares reports and recommendations for leadership, and supports strategic initiatives designed to improve overall occupational safety performance across the University. The Occupational Safety Manager serves as a visible leader and advocate for workplace safety and is expected to foster collaboration, accountability, and continuous improvement in support of Georgetown University's commitment to providing a safe and healthy learning and working environment. Work Interactions This position reports directly to the Director of Fire Prevention and Occupational Safety and serves as an integral member of the Environmental Health and Safety (EH&S) team within the Office of Public Safety. The Occupational Safety Manager works collaboratively with Planning and Facilities Management personnel, contractors, project managers, supervisors, employees, and other University stakeholders to support Georgetown University's commitment to providing a safe and healthy learning and working environment. The position provides technical consultation, regulatory guidance, training, and program support on occupational safety and health matters, including OSHA compliance, hazard identification, risk assessment, incident prevention, and safety program implementation. The incumbent serves as a trusted advisor to University leadership, departments, and project teams, helping identify workplace hazards, develop corrective actions, and implement effective risk mitigation strategies. The Occupational Safety Manager routinely collaborates with contractors, consultants, regulatory agencies, and internal partners to ensure compliance with applicable safety regulations, University policies, and industry best practices. Through inspections, audits, training, incident investigations, and continuous engagement with stakeholders, the position promotes a proactive safety culture, strengthens organizational accountability, and supports the successful execution of University operations, maintenance activities, and capital construction projects in a safe, compliant, and environmentally responsible manner. This position has been designated as On-Campus Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed to meet the university's evolving needs. Such review may necessitate changing a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Requirements and Qualifications Academic Level: Bachelor of Science degree in Occupational Safety, Safety Management, Construction Management, Industrial Hygiene, Environmental Health and Safety, Engineering, or a closely related field. Practical Experience: Requires at least five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in occupational safety, safety program management, construction safety, industrial safety, environmental health and safety, or a related discipline. Experience supporting a complex campus, institutional, healthcare, government, or commercial environment is preferred. Other Skills: Demonstrated knowledge of OSHA regulations, occupational safety principles, hazard identification, risk assessment methodologies, incident investigation techniques, and safety program implementation. Strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to effectively interact with employees, supervisors, contractors, project managers, and senior leadership. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Outlook. Experience using web-based reporting systems and inspection platforms. Ability to conduct safety inspections, audits, training programs, incident investigations, root cause analyses, and develop corrective action plans. Ability to interpret and apply regulatory requirements, technical standards, and University policies in a practical and effective manner. The incumbent is required to carry a smartphone and respond to inquiries as needed, including occasional off-hours support during emergencies, incident investigations, or other urgent operational needs. Preferred Qualifications:      • OSHA 30-Hour Construction Safety Certification      • Construction Health and Safety Technician (CHST) certification      • Experience developing and delivering occupational safety training programs      • Experience conducting incident investigations and root cause analyses      • Experience managing OSHA compliance programs, including Lockout/Tagout, Confined Space Entry, Fall Protection, Walking-Working Surfaces, and Personal Protective Equipment      • Experience working in higher education institutions is preferred Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such a review may necessitate a change to a position’s work mode designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode-of-work designations for staff positions are available on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation .   Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $66,783.00 - $126,720.23 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
