    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Washington-DC/Special-Police-Officer--6-opportunities-_JR26242": {
      "title": "Special Police Officer (6 opportunities)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Position #: P13170 Full-time: 40 hours Pay: $ 29.00 Location: Washington, DC The Special Police Officer provides services to protect the life, well-being, and property of students, faculty, staff, visitors, dignitaries, and other through policing, patrol, event security, investigation, and emergency response as outlined in general orders and special orders, as directed by superior officers. They support the university community by providing information and assistance, and is directly responsible to the patrol sergeant for fulfilling duties assigned performing patrol functions and specialized assignments according to all special and general orders in protection of life and property of Georgetown University. Interacting routinely with students, faculty, staff, parents, alumni, and neighbors, the Special Police Officer has additional duties that include but are not limited to:   ·         * Provides police and security services while protecting life and property, performing police patrol duties                                                                             while carrying batons and pepper spray. ·         * Patrols on foot, and/or motor vehicles, responding to emergencies and enforcing all United States, District of Columbia laws and University rules and regulations. ·         * Supports the university community by establishing and maintaining an environment in which all community members can go safely about their varied activities in the best interest of the university. ·         * Accurately and thoroughly prepares incident reports, safeguards information, evidence to ensure successful follow up, and resolution. ·         * Assists in the preliminary investigations of incidents as necessary, supporting and providing assistance to persons who have been victims of crime and attending court whenever necessary, regardless of other commitments. ·         * In the absence of the Communications Officer, answers all telephone call and responds to emergencies, burglar alarms, fire alarms, and requests for service. ·         * Conducts speaking presentations on topics, which have been identified through surveys and community feedback under the supervision of the shift supervisor, assistant supervisor, or coordinators. ·         * In furtherance of the university's higher education objectives, becomes well acquainted with members of the              University community. Work Interactions The Special Campus Police Officer is an integral part of University Safety. Errors can lead to damage to life, health and property.  Ineffective Public Safety at the University can have a severe impact on the reputation of the University as well.  As a visible representative of Public Safety the performance of the incumbent reflects positively or negatively on the entire department.  Furthermore as a liaison to various constituencies (students, faculty, staff, parents, alumni, visitors, neighbors) and external agencies (MPD, DCFD, FBI, USSS, etc).  The incumbent is often the fact of university safety. Incumbent interacts routinely with students, faculty, staff, parents, alumni, neighbors, MPD, DCFD and germs. Requirements and Qualifications ·         * High School diploma or equivalency ·         * Three years of general work experience with at least one year in security or a related field ·         * Must be eligible to obtain and maintain a campus police officer commission ·         * Possess and maintain a valid driver's license with no violations in the last three years and able to pass Georgetown University's Driver's Certification ·         * Ability to complete all required departmental trainings to include certification and arrest control tactics: Baton and QC-Based Aerosol Subject Restraint. (Training includes successful completion of the consortium of universities law enforcement academy, usually during the probation period or equivalent training and certification from a civilian or military law enforcement academy) ·         * Knowledge of criminal and civil law and police policies and procedures ·         * Completion of the Campus Law Enforcement Academy (250 hours) or an equivalent law enforcement academy within two (2) years of receiving a campus and university special police officer commission or has previously completed an equivalent law enforcement academy. Georgetown University will consider previous law enforcement or security training of two hundred and fifty (250) hours as substitution for meeting the stated Academy requirements.   Essential: The Special Police Officer is considered as essential under the University policy guidelines and therefore subject to be on call when necessary.   Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Executive-Coordinator--Office-of-the-Senior-Vice-President-and-Chief-Operating-Officer_JR27147": {
      "title": "Executive Coordinator, Office of the Executive Vice President and Chief Operating Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview This position provides key administrative functions and logistical support to the Executive Vice President and Chief Operating Officer (EVP/COO) and supports the Senior Associate VP and Chief of Staff (CoS) in the management and execution of strategic priorities. The Executive Coordinator is a cross-functional and self-directed team player who takes initiative, anticipates needs, ensures consistent high quality products and materials, and adapts to different situations. This position acts as a trusted advisor to the COO and CoS in office initiatives and must maintain the highest level of confidentiality with sensitive university matters.   This position is responsible for the day to day operations of the Office of the COO (OCOO) as they relate to scheduling, planning, meeting facilitation, and team task prioritization. This position interfaces with many internal and external colleagues and shares the responsibility of response coordination with the CoS. Additionally, this role executes and supports regular annual meetings and events as well as special projects as assigned.     Work Interactions and Work Mode Designation This position reports to the Senior Associate Vice President and Chief of Staff.   The Executive Coordinator interfaces directly with the COO and their direct reports. They manage the complex needs of the EVP/COO, and consequently, this position is critical to the proper functioning of the EVP/COO’s office. They must gain a firm grasp of the organization of the EVP/COO’s organization, and of the University more broadly and maintain a strong working relationship with offices throughout the University.   This is a highly visible position who interacts on a regular basis with internal as well as external constituencies including faculty, staff, students, alumni, University officials, local, national and international government officials and VIP dignitaries. As such, the professionalism with which this person performs her or his duties impacts the impression that faculty, staff, students and visitors have of the EVP/COO’s organization.   The Executive Coordinator interacts closely with all direct reports of the EVP/COO. Additionally, this position interacts with all levels of University leadership, counterparts in other offices, Board members and their representatives, and external colleagues.   This position has been designated as on-campus. Work on both the Hilltop Campus and the Capitol Campus each week will be required, depending on the schedule of the EVP/COO. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation .   Requirements and Qualifications This position requires a bachelor’s degree and three to five years of progressively complex administrative and customer service experience supporting senior leadership or C-level executive(s). Excellent written and oral communication skills, including grammar, spelling and composition are necessary. Candidate must have exceptionally strong organizational skills and analytical abilities, and must also demonstrate proven interpersonal skills and experience providing complex administrative support in a high profile environment with courtesy, professionalism, diplomacy, efficiency and confidentiality. Must be able to effectively manage and prioritize multiple tasks, understand stakeholder needs, and work under pressure. Experience with project management is preferred.   This position requires proficiency in the use of standard office equipment such as printers, copiers, faxes, and scanners as well as excellent skills with standard office productivity software including Gmail, Google Calendaring and other applications, Microsoft Office Suite (MSWord, Excel, Outlook and PowerPoint), including the use of advanced formatting of Google docs/Word, Google slides/PowerPoint, and Google sheets/Powerpoint.   The ideal candidate is extremely organized, flexible and creative, and able to work with a variety of personalities and constituencies to meet the demands of the job. She or he is a proactive self-starter who will also take direction and feedback from supervisors. This person proactively engages with, learns and communicates with evolving technologies to enhance the productivity of the EVP/COO and her or his team. The ideal candidate will be a trusted member of an essential team.   Sponsored Project Management (if applicable) n/a   http://hr.georgetown.edu/employment_services/costcentermanagers.html   Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $66,783.00 - $126,720.23 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/AI-Storyteller-and-Communications-Specialist_JR27155": {
      "title": "AI Storyteller and Communications Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The AI Storyteller and Communications Specialist is an embedded communications professional within the University's Office of Strategic Communications. Reporting to the Senior Director for Strategic Communication, the Specialist is responsible for developing and executing narrative strategies that highlight the research, educational programs, and daily activities of faculty, students, and staff throughout the entire university.  The immediate catalyst for this role is the Georgetown Initiative on AI Use Principles, launching in fall 2026. This role acts as the primary translator of advanced computational, technical, and ethical concepts for a general audience. They produce compelling written, digital, and social content that elevates the university’s  visibility among federal policymakers, national media, prospective students, and the broader scientific community.   Duties include but are not limited to: ●       Translate complex scientific and technical research into accessible articles, profiles, and media content for a general audience. ●       Communicate a unified narrative about diverse research, teaching, and service activities of Georgetown in the AI space. ●       Manage the university’s  digital AI presence, including website updates, social media campaigns, and monthly newsletters. ●       Work alongside the university’s media relations team to pitch research and practice developments to national journalists and prepare faculty for public and policy briefings. ●       Develop and implement communications strategies for major conferences, speaker series, and promotional events. ●       Collaborate with faculty and students to identify and highlight compelling, human-centric stories about AI initiatives. ●       Ensure all communications materials are accurate, stylistically consistent, and aligned with the university's brand guidelines. ●       Promote the ethical use of generative AI tools within the Office of Strategic Communications  through training and workflow integration.   Work Interactions The AI Storyteller and Communications Specialist operates within the Office of Strategic Communications , serving as a vital bridge between complex technical research activities and a broader, non-technical audience. This position reports directly to the Senior Director for Strategic Communication, working in close concert with University Media Relations, university faculty, and student researchers to amplify the impact of institutional initiatives. By translating dense, technical advancements into accessible, compelling narratives, the Specialist directly supports Georgetown University’s mission to foster innovation and public understanding. The role actively influences university communication strategy, ensuring alignment with university-wide brand standards while collaborating across teams to highlight human-centric stories and academic achievements.   Requirements and Qualifications Education : Bachelor's degree in Communications, Journalism, English, Science Writing, Computer Science, or a related field. Experience : Minimum of 3 to 5 years of professional experience in science writing, technology journalism, or strategic communications. Prior experience working within an academic research environment, federal laboratory, or a technology-policy think tank is highly preferred. Technical Translation Capability : Proven ability to translate advanced technical, mathematical, or scientific concepts into compelling narrative prose accessible to lay readers. (A writing sample demonstrating this translation is required for consideration). Project and Channel Management : Demonstrated experience managing professional websites, social media accounts, and digital email marketing platforms. Interpersonal and Collaborative Skills : Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and consultative skills, with a track record of building trusted relationships with academic researchers, administrative staff, and media professionals. Organizational Agility : Exceptional organizational skills, with a proven ability to manage multiple complex communications projects simultaneously under tight deadlines. Preferred Qualifications ●       Master's degree in Science Writing, Technology Policy, or a related field. ●       Foundational training or coursework in computational data science, artificial intelligence, machine learning, or cognitive neuroscience. ●       Practical experience working with graphic design and presentation software (e.g., Adobe Creative Suite, Figma, Canva, PowerPoint) to create infographics, slide decks, and digital assets. ●       Established connections with regional and national science, technology, and public policy journalists. ●       Demonstrated experience leveraging generative AI tools in real-world communication workflows (such as transcription, data analysis, copywriting, or visual design assistance). ●       Familiarity with Content Management Systems (like WordPress) and Marketing Automation solutions (like MailChimp)   Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as on-campus . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation .   Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $54,616.00 - $100,493.33 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Law-Center/Senior-Grants-and-Contracts-Administration_JR26598": {
      "title": "Senior Grants and Contracts Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview We are seeking a Grants & Contracts Administrator. This position is part of the Law Center’s Financial Affairs Team. The Grants & Contracts Administrator will work closely with Principal Investigators (PIs), Program Staff, Contracts, Human Resources, Joint Office of Research Administration (JORA), and Sponsor Projects Financial Operations (SPFO) to provide analysis and management of grants and revenue generating agreements. This involves oversight of the financial management of assigned cost centers with multi-year grants, gifts, contracts, and other funding. The current portfolio is over $31.5 million+. This includes ensuring grant management of all awards and financial operations of the Centers & Institutes are on schedule, within the scope of work and budget, and of the utmost quality. This person will ensure that reports are compatible with accounting practices and follow federal rules and regulations. They will also be responsible for ensuring that the PIs within their portfolio have the necessary financial analysis and guidance to make appropriate decisions throughout the lifetime of the award. Work Interactions As a member of the Law Center’s Finance Affairs Department, the staff member will provide support to the PIs of the Centers and Institutes and various groups and individuals within the organization who rely on and benefit from financial information to make informed business decisions through financial analyses (i.e. current policies and processes, actual performance vs. budget), preparation of financial data for distribution to management, as well as donors. The Grants and Contracts Administrator will work closely with ORS, SPFO, and the cash office to ensure the awards are set up properly, reports are turned in on time and payments are being credited to the appropriate award. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, or similar is required. Master degree preferred. 7-10 years of experience in an academic research environment or a non-profit organization. Expertise in grant and contract administration in a higher education or non-profit setting is preferred. Experience with budget preparation and budget justifications; ability to provide input to faculty members and proposal preparation staff on the appropriateness of budgeted items. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Remote. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $66,783.00 - $126,720.23 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit th