    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Pasquerilla-Healthcare-Center-1st-Floor/Lab-Manager_JR26725": {
      "title": "Lab Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The incumbent in this position performs Laboratory Management duties for the GUMC’s Clinical  Research Unit Laboratory at Georgetown University , ensuring compliance with regulatory standards, maintaining  high-quality specimen handling processes, and providing support for clinical research activities. The incumbent will  serve as the primary contact for all laboratory-related interactions, manage staff training, and contribute to clinical  support functions when the laboratory workload allows.  Additional duties include, but are not limited to:  Laboratory Management  Manage daily activities of the CRU laboratory Oversee processing, storing, and shipping of laboratory specimens Maintain ongoing tracking of all specimens stored in the CR  Monitor, maintain, and ensure proper function of all laboratory equipment Manage inventory and ordering of laboratory supplies Assume responsibility for on-call schedule for freezer alarm coverage (-80 freezers) Serve as the primary contact for all laboratory interactions with study teams Provide training and oversight to staff assisting in specimen processing Manage laboratory effort for community visits under the CTSA grant, collaborating with staff at Howard  University, Medstar and the VA as appropriate  Clinical Support   Assist nurses with clinical research and standard-of-care tasks when laboratory workload allows Perform vital signs, ECGs, and phlebotomy.  Assist with subject transport as needed.  Support pick-up and delivery of drugs from research and main pharmacy Collaborate directly with nursing staff on the CRU unit in patient care support and quality improvement  initiatives Work Interactions The Lab Manager provides laboratory support to the CRU and SEPCOM approved protocols.  The Lab Manager works as part of the CRU team and will report to CRU Nurse Manager, assisting with clinical  care and quality improvement initiatives on the unit. They will work directly with the nursing staff and clinical  research coordinators on the unit.  CRU Nurse Manager, in turn, is accountable to the Program Director for all clinical issues and the  Administrative Director of the CRU for all administrative matters.  The Lab Manager functions are performed in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations and  Georgetown University Medical Center’s philosophy, policies, procedures, and standards.   Requirements and Qualifications  Bachelor’s degree in a scientific discipline or equivalent experience Experience in laboratory management or clinical research laboratory operations Strong knowledge of specimen processing, storage, and shipping protocols Proficiency in laboratory equipment maintenance and inventory management Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with multidisciplinary teams IATA Certification  Preferred Qualifications  Advanced degree (MS or higher) in a scientific or health-related field.  Certification in clinical laboratory science or research compliance.  Prior experience in a clinical research setting.  Experience supervising or training staff.  Familiarity with freezer alarm systems and biorepository management.  Work Mode Designation   This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in  order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of  work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can  be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $41,926.00 - $65,090.00 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/125-E-St-NW-1st-Floor/Web-Manager--McCourt-School-of-Public-Policy_JR26724": {
      "title": "Web Manager, McCourt School of Public Policy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Web Manager develops and maintains the online presence for Georgetown’s McCourt School of Public Policy (McCourt). They are responsible for ongoing web development, content production, maintenance, meeting the university's accessibility policy, user experience design, and search engine and site speed performance optimizations for the primary web properties of McCourt. This position will work with stakeholders across McCourt and Georgetown University as a member of the McCourt Strategic Communications team to ensure that primary business objectives tied to online properties are successfully met and essential platform standards are maintained. The Web Manager will also track metrics and analytics and provide ongoing reporting and analysis and context on the main site’s performance. This position will be the primary point of contact for all content updates to and governance of the McCourt website. The Web Manager will work closely with the Web Services team in University Information Services (UIS) and Information Systems Technology (IST) to ensure McCourt’s website functionality and design adhere to the University’s central WordPress codebase. Any front-end development in the central CMS (WordPress) will follow all Web Services code standards and processes. The candidate will monitor Google Analytics (GA4), Siteimprove, and other server and site performance tools to maintain Section 508 compliance and core website performance standards.  The McCourt School website and other web properties represent cornerstones of our brand and act as the hub for all earned, owned and paid media efforts, prospective student engagement, current student and faculty communications, and alumni community engagement. The Web Manager will be a nimble, creative web professional with a passion for advancing the mission of a nonprofit university in the digital space. Work Interactions The Web Manager reports to the McCourt Director of Communications and works closely and collaboratively with the central McCourt Strategic Communications team, the McCourt Dean’s Office and other stakeholders across McCourt and Georgetown University, including academic and research faculty and staff. The Web Manager will also interact with members of the MarTech team (a central team at Georgetown whose work focuses on the intersection of marketing and technology) on web updates related to search engine optimization (SEO) and McCourt’s paid marketing activities. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Minimum of 5 years of relevant professional work experience in website content management, front-end programming, and/or digital marketing Strong experience with at least one enterprise web content management system, preferably WordPress Intermediate knowledge of HTML and CSS and their application within a centrally-managed WordPress environment Experience ensuring and maintaining Section 508 web accessibility in compliance with WCAG 2.2 Experience in responsive web design and mobile-first methodologies Excellent written and oral communication skills  Fluency in the use of design software for web development, such as Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, Dreamweaver, Experience Designer and/or Figma Strong organizational, project and time management skills  Ability to work both collaboratively in a team environment and independently with minimal supervision Proficiency in Microsoft Office and Google Workspace and using Google Analytics as a diagnostic tool for site performance and SEO Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of JavaScript programming language, particularly jQuery Familiarity with PHP programming Familiarity with SiteImprove as a diagnostic tool for site performance Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate changing a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s work mode designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $47,586.00 - $87,558.13 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
