    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Edward-B-Williams-Law-Library-1st-Floor/Digital-Initiatives-Librarian_JR26675": {
      "title": "Digital Initiatives Librarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Digital Initiatives Librarian, Law Library, Georgetown University Job Overview The Digital Initiatives Librarian is responsible for the creation, ingest, management, and preservation of the Georgetown Law Library’s digital assets. Reporting to the Head of Digital Initiatives, this position advises and develops local standards and identifies priorities for digitization. As an experienced member of the Digital Initiatives Department, this position handles complex digitization projects, and refines new digitization and ingest workflows. The incumbent works with the Head of Digital Initiatives to develop cohesive metadata standards for digital collections and assets, is responsible for planning and executing database maintenance projects and manages standards for bulk import and export of digital objects. This position assists in managing the Georgetown Law Library’s digital repository, DigitalGeorgetown, and serves as a point of contact for its shared development with campus libraries. Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Ensure access to digital collections through the Law Library’s digital repository and help develop workflows for ingest. Develop detailed metadata standards and workflows for digital collections. Oversee production-level digitization of Law Library materials including developing workflows for staff and students. Coordinate and plan digital preservation activities. Collaborate with Law Library staff to plan and prioritize digitization projects. Work Interactions The Digital Initiatives Librarian reports to the Head of Digital Initiatives. This position works closely with other members of the department including the Digital Initiatives Coordinator, the Digital Initiatives Assistant, and student workers. In addition, this position will interact with the Law Center Archivist, Head of Special Collections, and Digital Repository and Preservation Librarian at the University Library. Requirements and Qualifications Master’s Degree in Library and Information Science (or equivalent). Five to eight (5-8) years of library experience. Experience with digitization best practices and workflows, including the use of large-scale scanning equipment, image editing software, and inventory control procedures. Experience with institutional repository systems, including storing, organizing, securing, and sharing digital assets. Experience managing multiple concurrent digitization projects. Experience using digital imaging and post-processing software, such as Adobe Photoshop and Adobe Bridge. Knowledge of descriptive metadata schemas such as Dublin Core, MARC, MODS, or METS. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability to solve technical problems, implement new equipment and software, and apply technical standards for digitization. Experience in working with data from an Integrated Library System. Experience in an academic library in a university setting. Knowledge of digital preservation systems and best practices. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Please submit a cover letter and resume.  Preferably these documents should be combined into a single PDF. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $54,616.00 - $100,493.33 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
