    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/111-Massachusetts-Ave-4th-Floor/Operations-and-Marketing-Coordinator_JR26642": {
      "title": "Operations and Marketing Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Operations & Marketing Coordinator plays a dual strategic and administrative role as the operational backbone and the welcoming face of the Capitol Applied Learning Labs (CALL), Georgetown University. This position is uniquely positioned at the intersection of student engagement, community building, and operational strategy. Beyond managing daily HR, financial, and spatial operations, the Coordinator serves as a key brand ambassador, actively fostering a vibrant, inclusive CALL community. This front-facing role engages directly with prospective and current students, alumni, faculty, practitioners, and campus-wide partners. The ideal candidate pairs a passion for community building and student success with a meticulous, high-level attention to detail necessary for managing academic contracts, budgets, and public-facing digital media. Duties include but are not limited to : Serve as the primary point of contact and welcoming presence to actively build a vibrant, inclusive CALL community among prospective/current students, alumni, faculty, and external practitioners. Web & Digital Communications Management: Meticulously maintain and update the CALL website and blogs using WordPress, ensuring all public-facing information and digital brand assets are accurate and engaging. Contract & HR Administration: Partner with the Provost’s Office to execute and track complex faculty and practitioner contracts, while managing onboarding and HR transactions for staff and independent contractors. Strategic Marketing & Recruitment: Author, design, and distribute digital marketing campaigns, newsletters, social media content, and printed collateral to drive student recruitment and program visibility. Academic Operations & Enrollment Support: Collaborate closely with university registrar and scheduling teams to coordinate course registration, manage classroom scheduling, and facilitate seamless student enrollment. Support budget planning, track instructional costs, manage the unit ProCard under strict university compliance policies, and perform monthly budget reconciliations with the MCFO. Supervise, hire, and approve hours for a team of 5+ undergraduate student workers, while managing physical office operations and supply procurement. Work Interactions The Operations and Marketing Coordinator will work under direct supervision of the CALL Director. This position will work closely with other CALL and GU staff to complete administrative functions related to specific projects and to coordinate meetings, agendas, and related materials. This position will also maintain relationships with HR, MCFO (Main Campus Finance Office), and Provost’s Office to complete HR and financial transactions. The position will also serve as manager and supervise a team of 5+ undergraduate student workers that will work on various CALL projects. Requirements and Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s Degree required; Master’s Degree (conferred or in progress) preferred. Experience: 2–3 years of professional work experience, ideally in higher education, student affairs, hospitality, or a fast-paced, start-up-like environment. Attention to Detail: Exceptional organizational skills with a proven track record of handling high-stakes tasks like contract tracking, website maintenance, and financial reconciliation flawlessly. Interpersonal & Communication Skills: Outstanding verbal and written communication skills; comfort serving as a high-energy, front-facing representative to diverse audiences including students, executive leadership, and external practitioners. Marketing Savvy: Experience utilizing traditional and digital marketing, content marketing, and social media platforms to build brand engagement. Technical Literacy: Proficiency with WordPress (or equivalent content management systems) for website maintenance and updates. Experience working with database management software for data tracking and operational organization. Experience with using Canva, Adobe, and/or other marketing platforms for digital content creation. Literacy with Microsoft Office applications, including Word and Excel, and Google Suite applications, like Gmail, Google Docs, and Google Sheets. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $44,022.00 - $73,406.80 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
